SUMMARY:Pain and Its Killers: What a New Class of Non-Opioid Pain Medicine 
 Could Mean for Society
DESCRIPTION:Can a new painkiller bring relief to people without the risk of
  addiction?\n\nAfter two decades without innovation\, a breakthrough momen
 t arrived: Last year\, the FDA approved Journavx™ (suzetrigine)\, the fi
 rst new class of non-opioid pain medicine in more than 20 years. Early cli
 nical trials show it delivers relief comparable to opioids without the add
 iction risk. For millions living with chronic pain and a nation still grap
 pling with the opioid crisis\, this isn’t just medical news. It’s…\n
 \nhttps://www.creativephl.org/arts-event/pain-and-its-killers-what-a-new-c
 lass-of-non-opioid-pain-medicine-could-mean-for-society/
